  "theoryOfChange": "World Central Kitchen (WCK) operates with a defined model focused on quick action, leveraging local resources, and real-time adaptation to provide fresh meals in response to humanitarian, climate, and community crises. Their approach emphasizes mobilizing with urgency, partnering with local organizations, restaurants, and food trucks, and prioritizing the purchase of local ingredients to support regional economies. WCK's 'Culinary Standards' document outlines seven core culinary commitments to the communities they serve, including culturally appropriate food, food safety, and environmental sustainability, along with performance indicators for practitioners and partners. They also detail their 'food relief model' which allows them to respond immediately, locally, and at scale. This framework is further evidenced by their 'WCK Way' documents, which highlight their operational strategies and impact, and their 'operating model' which sets an example of empathy in action.",
